{"name":"Dimple","hex":"#e9808b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dimple","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small depression or indentation in a surface.","A small natural depression on the skin, especially on the face near the corners of the mouth."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form a small indentation in (something).","To form a dimple (noun sense 1.1) in one's face by smiling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dimple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dimple","blocks":[{"text":"A dimple, also called a gelasin, and a fovea buccalis, is a small natural indentation in the flesh on a part of the human body, most notably in the cheek. Numerous cultures believe that cheek dimples are a good luck charm that entices people who perceive them as physically attractive, but they are also associated with heroism and innocence, which has been included in literature for many centuries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Miranda_Kerr_%286880801131%29.jpg/330px-Miranda_Kerr_%286880801131%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Different_dimple_shape.png/500px-Different_dimple_shape.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Different_dimple_shape.png/500px-Different_dimple_shape.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADifferent_dimple_shape.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Mouth_dimple_and_cheek_dimple.png/500px-Mouth_dimple_and_cheek_dimple.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Mouth_dimple_and_cheek_dimple.png/500px-Mouth_dimple_and_cheek_dimple.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMouth_dimple_and_cheek_dimple.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Woman_wearing_Isabelle_Gilbert%27s_Dimple_Maker_invention.jpg/500px-Woman_wearing_Isabelle_Gilbert%27s_Dimple_Maker_invention.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Woman_wearing_Isabelle_Gilbert%27s_Dimple_Maker_invention.jpg/500px-Woman_wearing_Isabelle_Gilbert%27s_Dimple_Maker_invention.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Isabelle Gilbert's (not pictured) Dimple Maker claimed to make permanent cheek dimples for women who desired them.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWoman_wearing_Isabelle_Gilbert's_Dimple_Maker_invention.jpg"}],"sounds":{"dimple":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/03/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dimple.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/03/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dimple.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dimple.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/03/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dimple.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dimple.wav.ogg"}]}}}